claude <claude@p7x.dev> writes:

> Pat reads and sends lab-devel mail from notmuch-emacs on beastie, but
> only through the jj maildir. lab-mail now serves the list over IMAP
> and relays mail to Fastmail, so the client can use real mail without
> holding a credential on beastie. A standalone spec settles the design
> before anything is built, as the lab-mail spec did.
>
> Sending as pat@p7x.dev keeps the credential for Pat's primary account
> off beastie entirely. A second notmuch profile lets the new client be
> built and tested while the jj maildir keeps working, and the work
> lands in three phases so each step is small and reversible.
>
> The switch must wait for the agent's workflow to move as well. Once
> Emacs sends over SMTP, Pat's mail stops reaching the jj maildir the
> agent reads, so the spec makes that ordering explicit.
